<title>USA: Merrill Lynch &amp; Co Q3 Sept 27 net rises.</title>
<headline>Merrill Lynch &amp; Co Q3 Sept 27 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr primary		$1.69		    $1.47</p>
<p> Shr diluted		$1.68		    $1.46</p>
<p> Net			331,000		  300,000</p>
<p> Total revs	   6,201,000		5,431,000</p>
<p> Net revs	     3,093,000		2,682,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary     189,200		  196,400</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted     190,600		  197,200</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>			9 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr primary		$5.91		    $3.95</p>
<p> Shr diluted		$5.89		    $3.90</p>
<p> Net		    1,174,000		  810,000</p>
<p> Total revs	  18,410,000	     16,220,000</p>
<p> Net revs	     9,735,000		7,652,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary     192,600		  196,300</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted     193,300		  198,800</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Net revenue figures include interest expenses.</p>
<p>Investment banking revenues $471 million vs $354 million in Q3, and $1.43 billion vs $938 million year-to-date.</p>
<p>Q3 effective tax rate 36.6 percent vs 38.1 percent.</p>
